.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
🎉️ **NEW**: [date-fns v3 is out!](https://blog.date-fns.org/v3-is-out/)

.PP

.PP
date-fns provides the most comprehensive, yet simple and consistent toolset for manipulating JavaScript dates in a browser & Node\&.js

.PP
👉 \fRDocumentation\fP

.PP
👉 \fRBlog\fP

.PP
.PP

.PP
It's like \fRLodash\fP for dates

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
It has \fR\fB200+ functions\fP for all occasions\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBModular\fP: Pick what you need\&. Works with webpack, Browserify, or Rollup and also supports tree-shaking\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBNative dates\fP: Uses existing native type\&. It doesn't extend core objects for safety's sake\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBImmutable & Pure\fP: Built using pure functions and always returns a new date instance\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBTypeScript\fP: The library is 100% TypeScript with brand-new handcrafted types\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBI18n\fP: Dozens of locales\&. Include only what you need\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRand many more benefits\fP
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { compareAsc, format } from "date\-fns";

format(new Date(2014, 1, 11), "yyyy\-MM\-dd");
//=> '2014\-02\-11'

const dates = [
  new Date(1995, 6, 2),
  new Date(1987, 1, 11),
  new Date(1989, 6, 10),
];
dates\&.sort(compareAsc);
//=> [
//   Wed Feb 11 1987 00:00:00,
//   Mon Jul 10 1989 00:00:00,
//   Sun Jul 02 1995 00:00:00
// ]
.fi
.PP

.PP
The library is available as an \fRnpm package\fP\&. To install the package run:

.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install date\-fns \-\-save
.fi
.PP
.SS "Docs"
\fRSee date-fns\&.org\fP for more details, API, and other docs\&.

.PP

